window.TEM8_TRANSCRIPTS = {"2025":{"A":[{"en":"Good morning, everyone.","t":95.52,"tOriginal":35,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":11},{"en":"Today, we're going to talk about working memory.","t":97.86,"tOriginal":36.5,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":12},{"en":"OK, what is working memory?","t":102.72,"tOriginal":40.4,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":13},{"en":"Working memory is that part of our consciousness that we are aware of at any given time of day.","t":104.42,"tOriginal":42.8,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":14},{"en":"In fact, you're doing it right now.","t":114.78,"tOriginal":52.1,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":15},{"en":"It's not something we can turn off.","t":116.56,"tOriginal":55.6,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":16},{"en":"If you turn it off, that's called a coma, loss of consciousness, right?","t":120.58,"tOriginal":59,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":17},{"en":"Now,What does our working memory contain?","t":127.08,"tOriginal":65.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":18},{"en":"First, it stores some immediate experiences and a little bit of knowledge.","t":130.56,"tOriginal":68.8,"tSource":"transcript-interpolated"},{"en":"Second, it allows us to reach back into our long-term memory and pull some of that in as we need it, mixes it, processes it in light of whatever our current goal is.","t":136.34,"tOriginal":74.6,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":19},{"en":"Please note the current goal isn't something like, I want to be the CEO in a big company or the top student in the class.","t":149.54,"tOriginal":91.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":20},{"en":"It's not something like this.","t":159.86,"tOriginal":103.5,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":21},{"en":"It's more common.","t":162.1,"tOriginal":106,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":22},{"en":"For example, I'd like that biscuit, or I need to figure out how to get to the railway station.","t":164.18,"tOriginal":107.4,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":23},{"en":"So in a word, working memory capacity is our ability to take what we know and use it in ways that allow us to satisfy our current goal.","t":171.9,"tOriginal":116.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":24},{"en":"Now,let's talk a bit more about working memory capacity.","t":182.48,"tOriginal":130.4,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":25},{"en":"Research in this field has a fairly long history, and it shows that working memory capacity has the following positive effects.","t":189.0,"tOriginal":135.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":26},{"en":"First, people with high working memory capacity tend to be good storytellers.","t":199.24,"tOriginal":145.6,"tSource":"transcript-interpolated"},{"en":"They tend to solve and do well on standardized tests, however important that is.","t":205.1,"tOriginal":151.5,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":27},{"en":"They are able to have high levels of writing ability.","t":212.28,"tOriginal":158.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":28},{"en":"They're also able to reason at high levels.","t":215.98,"tOriginal":163.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":29},{"en":"Second, working memory is great because it helps us to communicate in such ways.","t":219.6,"tOriginal":167.1,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":30},{"en":"We can have a conversation, and I can build a narrative around that, so I know where we've been and where we're going, and how to contribute to this conversation.","t":226.24,"tOriginal":174,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":31},{"en":"Third, it allows us to solve problems and do critical thinking.","t":237.55,"tOriginal":188.7,"tSource":"transcript-interpolated"},{"en":"For example, when we are in the middle of a meeting, we can listen to somebody's presentation, evaluate it, decide whether we like it or not, and ask follow-up questions.","t":241.7,"tOriginal":194.1,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":32},{"en":"All of that occurs within working memory.","t":256.76,"tOriginal":209.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":33},{"en":"Finally, our working memory also functions like this.","t":260.74,"tOriginal":212.6,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":34},{"en":"Suppose now we are shopping in the store, we often buy milk and egs and bread, when at the same time, what we are really looking for is vegetable and pork.","t":263.88,"tOriginal":216.6,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":35},{"en":"We need to make sure we’re getting what we're looking for on those everyday occasions.","t":266.12,"tOriginal":231.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":36},{"en":"Now,a central issue with working memory is that it's limited.","t":282.82,"tOriginal":239.6,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":37},{"en":"This means it's limited in capacity, limited in duration, limited in focus.","t":286.9,"tOriginal":244.9,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":38},{"en":"We tend to remember about four things.","t":295.32,"tOriginal":250.8,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":39},{"en":"Suppose we can remember those four things for about 10 to 20 seconds unless we do something with it, unless we process it, unless we apply it to something, unless we talk to somebody about it.","t":298.94,"tOriginal":254.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":40},{"en":"The problem that we have is that life now comes at us very quickly, and what we need to do is to take that abundant flow of experience and somehow extract meaning from it with a working memory, which is about the size of a pea.","t":319.06,"tOriginal":270.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":42},{"en":"But don't get me wrong at this point, working memory is truly awesome.","t":325.16,"tOriginal":293.4,"tSource":"transcript-interpolated"},{"en":"Working memory makes us investigate our current experience as we move forward, and it helps us to make sense of the world around us.","t":326.9,"tOriginal":299.8,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":43},{"en":"But I repeat, it does have certain limits.","t":345.94,"tOriginal":311.5,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":44},{"en":"So when we think about working memory, we have to realize that this limited capacity has lots of different impacts on us.","t":349.66,"tOriginal":315.4,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":45},{"en":"Have you ever walked from one room to another and then forgotten why you're there?","t":353.08,"tOriginal":326.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":46},{"en":"You do know the solution to that, right?","t":364.7,"tOriginal":333.5,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":47},{"en":"You go back to that original room.","t":366.8,"tOriginal":337.4,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":48},{"en":"We need to realize that working memory has a limited capacity.","t":370.76,"tOriginal":340.9,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":49},{"en":"So what I want to do now is to talk a little bit about a couple of strategies here, and these will be really important because you are now in an information era.","t":375.64,"tOriginal":346.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":50},{"en":"Now the first part of this is that we need to process our existence, our life immediately.","t":386.64,"tOriginal":362.4,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":52},{"en":"This means that we need to process what’s going on the moment it happens,not 10 minutes later,not a week later, but at the moment.","t":388.16,"tOriginal":370.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":53},{"en":"So during a meeting or conversation, we need to think about, well, do I agree with him?","t":404.28,"tOriginal":383.4,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":54},{"en":"What's missing?","t":411.02,"tOriginal":391.8,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":55},{"en":"What would I like to know now?","t":412.52,"tOriginal":392.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":56},{"en":"It's a way of processing what's going on so that we can use it later.","t":415.02,"tOriginal":396.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":57},{"en":"Second, we also need to repeat it.","t":419.82,"tOriginal":403.5,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":58},{"en":"We need to practice.","t":421.02,"tOriginal":406.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":59},{"en":"So we need to think about it here.","t":425.66,"tOriginal":408.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":60},{"en":"In between, we want to talk to people about it.","t":427.48,"tOriginal":412.8,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":61},{"en":"We're going to write it down, and when you get home, pull out those notes and think about them and end up practicing over time.","t":434.26,"tOriginal":417.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":63},{"en":"The third thing is, we need to think elaboratively and we need to think illustratively.","t":440.08,"tOriginal":429.9,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":64},{"en":"Oftentimes, we think that we have to relate new knowledge to prior knowledge.","t":449.26,"tOriginal":437.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":65},{"en":"How can we do it?","t":454.96,"tOriginal":443.6,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":66},{"en":"We can take all of our prior knowledge, or existence, and wrap it around that new knowledge and make all of these connections, and then it becomes more meaningful.","t":456.84,"tOriginal":446.1,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":67},{"en":"The fourth important strategy that I use is imagery.","t":469.38,"tOriginal":460.3,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":68},{"en":"We are built for images.","t":473.62,"tOriginal":464.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":69},{"en":"We need to take advantage of that.","t":476.4,"tOriginal":467.1,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":70},{"en":"Think about things in images, write things down that way.","t":479.38,"tOriginal":470.6,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":71},{"en":"If you read a book, pull things up.","t":482.62,"tOriginal":475.5,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":72},{"en":"For example, I just got through reading A Dream of the Red Chamber, and I have a perfect idea of what Lin Daiyu looks like in my mind, my own version of Lin Daiyu.","t":487.22,"tOriginal":479.4,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":73},{"en":"Now, the last strategy.","t":499.28,"tOriginal":496,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":74},{"en":"We humans are meaning-making machines.","t":502.2,"tOriginal":498,"tSource":"transcript-interpolated"},{"en":"It's what we do.","t":506.44,"tOriginal":500.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":75},{"en":"We try to make meaning out of everything that happens to us.","t":506.94,"tOriginal":502.9,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":76},{"en":"Here, organization helps.","t":513.76,"tOriginal":508.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":77},{"en":"So we need to structure what we're doing in ways that make sense.","t":515.22,"tOriginal":510.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":78},{"en":"If we are providing knowledge and experience, we need to put it in some kind of order.","t":518.72,"tOriginal":516.6,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":79},{"en":"And we also need support.","t":521.6,"tOriginal":524.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":80},{"en":"The support may come in asking people questions, giving them a sheet of paper that has an organizational chart on it, or has some guiding images.","t":527.44,"tOriginal":527.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":81},{"en":"So we need to support it.","t":538.38,"tOriginal":540.1,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":82},{"en":"OK, to recap today's lecture, we've talked about what working memory is, its functions, roles,and limitations, and the strategies to be used to offset the limitations.","t":543.16,"tOriginal":543,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":84},{"en":"In our next lecture, we are going to talk about the functions of our long-term memory.","t":558.02,"tOriginal":556.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":85},{"en":"Thank you.","t":561.29,"tOriginal":564.5,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":86}],"B":[{"en":"Good evening, everybody.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":833.42,"tOriginal":770,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":100},{"en":"Today, we are delighted to have invited Allen Lee, a consultant in Silicon Valley to tell us his latest book Rest:Why You Get More Done When You Work Less.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":836.58,"tOriginal":772,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":101},{"en":"This book is an empirical argument in favour of more limited working hours and greater understanding of the benefits of active rest as a means of raising creativity and productivity.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":849.06,"tOriginal":791.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":102},{"en":"Well, Allen.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":865.86,"tOriginal":811.8,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":103},{"en":"Thanks.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":866.57,"tOriginal":813.1,"tSource":"transcript-interpolated"},{"en":"I am very pleased to meet you all.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":867.28,"tOriginal":814.4,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":104},{"en":"Allen, what made you decide to write the book?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":869.96,"tOriginal":819.7,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":105},{"en":"I've been working as a consultant in Silicon Valley for about 20 years, and a few years ago, after lots of long projects and multitasking and travel, I started to feel the classic effects of burnout.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":873.96,"tOriginal":825.7,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":106},{"en":"My first response to this was to try to fit more into the day, to try to work harder.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":876.96,"tOriginal":848.9,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":107},{"en":"But when I was away on sabbatical at the Blue Hill Research Center, I found that in the three months there I got an enormous amount of stuff done and did an awful lot of really serious thinking.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":898.88,"tOriginal":861.5,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":108},{"en":"And whether you believe it or not, I also had what felt like an amazingly leisurely life.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":910.64,"tOriginal":886.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":109},{"en":"Oh, that's unbelievable.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":921.9,"tOriginal":898,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":110},{"en":"I didn't feel the constant pressure to look busy or the stress that I had when I was consulting.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":924.5,"tOriginal":900,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":111},{"en":"And it made me think that maybe we had this idea about the relationship between working hours and productivity backward.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":931.98,"tOriginal":912.6,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":112},{"en":"And we should make more time in our lives for leisure in the classic Greek sense, not playing a lot of video games.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":939.95,"tOriginal":925.9,"tSource":"transcript-interpolated"},{"en":"So,up until you wrote the book, you thought the more you worked the more productive you were?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":949.06,"tOriginal":941.1,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":113},{"en":"Yes, there was a straight line going up.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":956.08,"tOriginal":953.1,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":114},{"en":"More hours equalled more productivity.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":960.54,"tOriginal":958.4,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":115},{"en":"This is an assumption, which is a mistake, really, that we've been making for a very long time.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":963.76,"tOriginal":961.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":116},{"en":"And now there's more than a century's worth of research that shows overwork in the long run is bad for people and organisations and also bad for productivity.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":970.7,"tOriginal":973.6,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":117},{"en":"Overwork is something that can be sustained for a few weeks but after that, well, you start creating more problems than you solve.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":975.86,"tOriginal":992.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":118},{"en":"We're now living in a digital age where theoretically there is a great deal of flexibility in our modes of work but at the same time we're more connected than ever to work.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":995.06,"tOriginal":1007.4,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":119},{"en":"Can you foresee employers enforcing more detachment from work?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":1008.78,"tOriginal":1029.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":120},{"en":"Well, I think we have tended to be less critical and questioning of the virtues of new technologies, particularly communications technologies, than perhaps we should.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":1012.72,"tOriginal":1035.3,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":121},{"en":"However, after a generation's experience with emails, a decade's experience with smartphones,we are discovering that these technologies do not automatically make us more productive or give us more time with our kids.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":1027.34,"tOriginal":1051.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":122},{"en":"Rather, they have tended to grind work down to a fine powder that spreads out right through our day.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":1044.62,"tOriginal":1073.8,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":123},{"en":"Is it possible to dial this back?","sp":"M","part":1,"t":1052.84,"tOriginal":1086.4,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":124},{"en":"The answer is there are companies that are already doing so.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":1055.6,"tOriginal":1091,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":125},{"en":"They have been limiting email contact in the evening and reducing the length of the working day.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":1060.1,"tOriginal":1098.3,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":126},{"en":"Because you can have people doing an eight-hour day rather than a 10-hour day and still have people doing good work and being productive, I think these companies show that it is not inevitable that communications technologies have to keep us connected 24 hours every working day plus the weekend.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":1076.64,"tOriginal":1109.6,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":127},{"en":"Historically there have been very different working cultures in different places.","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1185.74,"tOriginal":1142.8,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":137},{"en":"Some have longer holidays and shorter working weeks, while others are just the opposite.","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1191.64,"tOriginal":1150.1,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":138},{"en":"What do you think?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1198.4,"tOriginal":1159.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":139},{"en":"Well, when you look at the statistics on the relationship between working hours and productivity in the world, one of the striking things you find is that it's not as clear and linear a relationship as you think.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1198.9,"tOriginal":1162,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":140},{"en":"Countries like Mexico have longer working weeks and longer working years than some European countries, but they have lower productivity rates.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1215.84,"tOriginal":1187.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":141},{"en":"But the idea that it's important to maintain better work-life balance turns out in the long run to have a lot going for it.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1223.06,"tOriginal":1201.1,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":142},{"en":"You say in your book, rest can be defined in wider terms than that…","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1235.94,"tOriginal":1217.7,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":143},{"en":"Yes, we often think of rest as a negative term defined by absence of work, but it's really much more than that.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1241.14,"tOriginal":1227,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":144},{"en":"The counterintuitive discovery is that many of the most restorative kinds of rest are actually active.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1250.3,"tOriginal":1241.6,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":145},{"en":"Things like exercise or walks or serious, engaging hobbies do more for you than sitting on the couch watching television.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1259.34,"tOriginal":1252.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":146},{"en":"The kind of rest, like watching TV, playing video games, certainly has its place but active rest delivers the greatest benefits.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1269.84,"tOriginal":1265.5,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":147},{"en":"It also provides occasion for creative reflection.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1280.72,"tOriginal":1279.4,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":149},{"en":"So,in your book, you talk about the importance of “deep play”.","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1285.1,"tOriginal":1284,"tSource":"asr2","tCueNo":151},{"en":"Is that a recognised psychological concept?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1290.2,"tOriginal":1292,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":152},{"en":"The term deep play comes originally from Jeremy Bentham but a cultural anthropologist called Clifford Geertz popularised it.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1293.84,"tOriginal":1296,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":153},{"en":"People who are really ambitious and think about their work an awful lot will have these hobbies that look like they absorb gigantic amounts of time and energy.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1304.74,"tOriginal":1307.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":154},{"en":"There are all kinds of different terms for roughly the same kind of thing, that is, serious leisure.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1316.54,"tOriginal":1326.5,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":155},{"en":"The fact that there is no one term for this activity reflects the fact that there is no clear idea of its importance.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1324.04,"tOriginal":1338.4,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":157},{"en":"But what I came to see is that these kind of activities, like, for example, mountain climbing, have a deeper value that makes the investment of time and energy worthwhile.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1331.5,"tOriginal":1353.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":158},{"en":"Then what about sleep?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1345.38,"tOriginal":1373.6,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":159},{"en":"If you don't care about your mental development or your body, then forget about sleep.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1345.98,"tOriginal":1376.2,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":160},{"en":"Otherwise sleep is the original rest.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1354.12,"tOriginal":1386.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":161},{"en":"Scientists still haven't found the one thing that explains why if you have a nervous system you need to sleep, and even if you don't have a nervous system you need to sleep—plants do something similar.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1358.12,"tOriginal":1390.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":162},{"en":"Sleep is incredibly important for brain maintenance.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1373.9,"tOriginal":1414.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":165},{"en":"When we sleep the brain takes time to clear out plaques and toxins that have built up during the hours we are awake.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1377.54,"tOriginal":1419.3,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":166},{"en":"Even though we're not aware of it, sleep also helps us push forward on questions and problems we're working on during our waking hours.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1377.94,"tOriginal":1434.6,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":167},{"en":"What's the most surprising insight or fact you came across in your research?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1394.78,"tOriginal":1450.5,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":169},{"en":"The biggest thing that I took away from this book is it's completely changed the way that I think about creativity.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1400.68,"tOriginal":1459.1,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":170},{"en":"I used to have a romantic notion in the 19th-century sense that creativity was something that was irrational and chaotic, that proceeds from a bolt from the blue, where you get inspired and then start working.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1403.3,"tOriginal":1473.1,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":171},{"en":"And what you see in lots of creative lives is a completely different model of working.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1417.66,"tOriginal":1497.6,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":172},{"en":"As the saying goes: “Inspiration exists but it has to find you at work.”People who have long creative lives, who do really great work for decades,they don't get inspired and start work.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1438.22,"tOriginal":1508.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":174},{"en":"They start work and get inspired.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1444.0,"tOriginal":1530.8,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":175},{"en":"And they do this every day.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1448.56,"tOriginal":1534.7,"tSource":"transcript-interpolated"},{"en":"That was a real revelation.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1453.24,"tOriginal":1538.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":176},{"en":"OK, thank you very much, Allen, for joining us tonight.","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1456.32,"tOriginal":1542,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":178},{"en":"Pleasure.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1459.86,"tOriginal":1548.7,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":179}]},"2026":{"A":[{"en":"Ladies and gentlemen, good morning.","t":9,"tOriginal":35,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Thank you very much for inviting me to speak at this conference.","t":12.2,"tOriginal":37.9,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Today, I'll share with you some of my observations of China's modernization journey.","t":19.7,"tOriginal":44.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"There is no better way to understand China's development trajectory than by traveling across the country.","t":27.9,"tOriginal":52.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"A few weeks ago, I found myself on a high-speed train from Sanmenxia in Henan province to Beijing.","t":38,"tOriginal":61.5,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"For nearly 1,000 kilometers rivers, communities, and vast plains flashed past the window at 350 km per hour.","t":50.1,"tOriginal":72.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Over the past 15 years, China has built 48,000 km of high-speed rail, roughly the distance from Beijing to Paris and back three times.","t":60.4,"tOriginal":81.7,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"This is more than a transportation network; it is a vivid reminder of what long-term planning and farsighted leadership can achieve.","t":75,"tOriginal":94.9,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Then what is the strategic context?","t":86,"tOriginal":107.6,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"As the world enters an era of geopolitical uncertainty, China is preparing for the next five years of its modernization journey.","t":89,"tOriginal":111,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"The world is confronting climate disruption, slowing growth and dangerous fragmentation.","t":99.3,"tOriginal":123.1,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Some countries shift dramatically with each election cycle.","t":104.7,"tOriginal":129.5,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Many others are distracted or divided or changing leaders in a rotating circus.","t":108.6,"tOriginal":134.1,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"China, in contrast, is laying out a long-term road map with unusual clarity.","t":115,"tOriginal":141.6,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"What has become increasingly evident is that China views the coming stage of development as driven by two transformative forces: green technology and artificial intelligence.","t":124,"tOriginal":149.6,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"One provides clean and abundant energy, and the other provides the intelligence needed to use that energy wisely.","t":140.3,"tOriginal":164,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Together, they form the basis of a new economic model that is greener, smarter and more sustainable.","t":152,"tOriginal":174.4,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"These two forces enrich the connotations of what Chinese policymakers call “New Quality Productive Forces,” which refers to a broad upgrade of the nation's industrial and technological foundations.","t":162.2,"tOriginal":184.2,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"The biotech and medicine revolution may be a third pillar.","t":179,"tOriginal":200.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Their influence will extend far beyond China's borders.","t":185,"tOriginal":206.1,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"First, China's green transformation is already visible across the country.","t":189.7,"tOriginal":210.7,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"An enterprise in Guangdong province has developed a wind turbine with a capacity of 50 megawatts, which is the world's largest floating offshore wind turbine.","t":195.6,"tOriginal":216.5,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"It only takes 20 of these turbines to produce 1 GW of electricity, a scale that would have been unimaginable a decade ago.","t":209.7,"tOriginal":230.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Meanwhile, Tongwei Solar, one of the world's largest solar companies headquartered in Chengdu, has produced more solar cells than any other nation has installed in its history.","t":222,"tOriginal":242.4,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Far to the northwest, in Gansu province, China has commissioned a groundbreaking solar-thermal plant, which is made up of 27,000 computer-guided mirrors.","t":236.5,"tOriginal":257.9,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Each mirror follows the sun with remarkable precision and concentrates its energy onto molten salt that retains heat long after sunset.","t":249,"tOriginal":271.2,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"This makes it possible to generate clean electricity throughout the night and helps overcome one of the largest limitations of solar power.","t":261.7,"tOriginal":283.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"These projects reveal the extraordinary scale at which China is now developing renewable infrastructure.","t":275,"tOriginal":296,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"They are also one major reason why the world has generated more electricity from renewables than from coal for the first time.","t":282.9,"tOriginal":304,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Within China, the green surge is also reshaping the structure of the economy.","t":295.6,"tOriginal":316.7,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Clean industries such as solar, wind, electric vehicles and batteries are emerging as new engines of growth at a time when real estate and traditional heavy industry can no longer play the same role.","t":303,"tOriginal":324.2,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"They are generating high-quality jobs and narrowing the gap between coastal and inland regions.","t":323.2,"tOriginal":343.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"They also give China a stronger foundation for the next technological wave.","t":332.1,"tOriginal":352.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"A country that can increasingly power its factories, transportation and cities with sun and wind is far better positioned to power data centers, quantum computing and intelligent infrastructure.","t":339.3,"tOriginal":359.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"The green transition is therefore not only about reducing emissions.","t":356,"tOriginal":375.5,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"It is also about building the physical backbone for the next stage of development.","t":361.4,"tOriginal":381.2,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"And then this brings us to another highlight, that is the AI revolution.","t":369.2,"tOriginal":389.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"If the green transformation provides the hardware of the future, AI provides the software.","t":376.4,"tOriginal":396.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"While companies of other countries focus on pushing the boundaries of human-like intelligence and scaling foundation models at extraordinary cost, China is doing something different.","t":384,"tOriginal":404.8,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"While investing heavily in frontier AI, China places greater emphasis on the broad integration of AI across every sector of the economy.","t":399.5,"tOriginal":419.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"AI in China is not limited to research labs.","t":412.6,"tOriginal":432.5,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"It is already reshaping transportation, healthcare, manufacturing, logistics, education, environmental management and public services.","t":418,"tOriginal":437.7,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Its development is practical, grounded and highly integrated.","t":430.6,"tOriginal":445.7,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"China's advantage lies in what analysts describe as “Industrial Maximalism”.","t":438,"tOriginal":450.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Rather than concentrating investment in a few selected sectors, China builds overlapping industrial ecosystems, for example, solar interacting with batteries, batteries with electric vehicles, electric vehicles with robotics, robotics with AI and so on.","t":447,"tOriginal":456.1,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"The country does not attempt to pick technological winners at the outset.","t":468.9,"tOriginal":475.7,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"It creates the conditions for fierce competition and rapid iteration.","t":476.6,"tOriginal":482.6,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Entire industrial chains grow together, learning from one another and driving each other forward.","t":483.1,"tOriginal":488.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"This approach explains how China moved from being unable to produce world-class combustion engines to becoming the global leader in electric vehicles.","t":492,"tOriginal":496.4,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"When confronted with fundamental technological barriers, China chose not to continue old battles.","t":506.4,"tOriginal":509.7,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"It created new terrain.","t":514.5,"tOriginal":517.2,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"The United Nations Industrial Development Organization expects China to represent incredibly 45 percent of global manufacturing by 2030.","t":517,"tOriginal":519.5,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Now, let me conclude my speech.","t":531,"tOriginal":528.7,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"In this world, China is betting on planning, continuity and collective ambition.","t":533,"tOriginal":532.2,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"If it succeeds, and I believe it will, the benefits will reach far beyond its borders.","t":539.9,"tOriginal":539.1,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"They will help guide humanity toward a cleaner, more prosperous, and more harmonious future.","t":549,"tOriginal":548.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Thank you.","t":557,"tOriginal":556.3,"tSource":"word-anchor"}],"B":[{"en":"We are here today with Nelson Leach on our show, who is many things, like acting, film directing, script writing, teaching… Today we want to talk to him about his writing.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":827,"tOriginal":760,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Good evening, Nelson.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":843.4,"tOriginal":784.6,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Good evening.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":845,"tOriginal":787,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Let's start at the very beginning.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":846,"tOriginal":788.6,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"What is the first story you ever wrote?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":848.5,"tOriginal":793.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"You'll be surprised… my first story was the beginning of a novel which I wrote when I was around 11 years old.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":852,"tOriginal":799.7,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"I handwrote at least 50 pages on a notebook that I kept inside my desk drawer in my bedroom.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":860.9,"tOriginal":816.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Someway, though, it got lost.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":868.5,"tOriginal":830.7,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"I have no idea what happened to it.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":870.6,"tOriginal":834.6,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"That's a pity!","sp":"W","part":1,"t":874,"tOriginal":841,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"After growing up, what movies or stories inspired your creativity?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":875.4,"tOriginal":843.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Can you tell us a bit?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":880.1,"tOriginal":851.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Well, from early on, it was Greek mythology.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":883,"tOriginal":856.1,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"I was, and still am in a lot of ways, obsessed with it.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":886.9,"tOriginal":862.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Then I moved to classic literature (Shakespeare, Dickens, just to name a couple) and then films.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":893.3,"tOriginal":872.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"But Greek mythology still impresses me the most.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":901.1,"tOriginal":885.5,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"What, what about modern literature?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":905,"tOriginal":891.8,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"It doesn't inspire you?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":908.3,"tOriginal":895.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"I have to admit that I don't read anything “modern”…","sp":"M","part":1,"t":911,"tOriginal":899,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Okay, now imagine that you were not a well-known writer.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":915,"tOriginal":906.9,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"How would you make directors and producers read your screenplay?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":920.7,"tOriginal":915.6,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Well, I have never had any problems with that myself, so I don't really know what to say.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":926,"tOriginal":923.6,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"However, some friends of mine have told me how they do it.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":933.2,"tOriginal":937.9,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"So, how do they do it?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":938,"tOriginal":947.4,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Well, according to them, you must follow the work of other writers and directors that you find interesting.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":940,"tOriginal":952.2,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Then get in touch with them through the internet.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":948.6,"tOriginal":966.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"In this digital age, it's easier than ever to contact people: e-mails, webpages, you know.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":953,"tOriginal":973.6,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Once you've made contact, you can send them your script directly.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":960.7,"tOriginal":986.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Let's move on to another question.","sp":"W","part":1,"t":966,"tOriginal":995,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"What experiences from your life influence your characters?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":969.9,"tOriginal":999.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Every person I know, have ever known or even run into for an instant.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":975,"tOriginal":1006.1,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"My family.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":982.5,"tOriginal":1017.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"My friends.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":983.5,"tOriginal":1018.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"My relationships.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":984.6,"tOriginal":1020.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"I sit around public places and listen to other people's conversations.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":985.7,"tOriginal":1022,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"If they interest me, I sometimes record them or write down things they say.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":991.6,"tOriginal":1030.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Then how emotionally involved are you with the characters you create?","sp":"W","part":1,"t":999,"tOriginal":1041.9,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Oh, they live with me the entire time I'm writing them.","sp":"M","part":1,"t":1007,"tOriginal":1050.6,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"I can be out with friends, at a dinner, on a date and I'm sitting there thinking to myself, well, how would my character react now?","sp":"M","part":1,"t":1016.5,"tOriginal":1059.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"They're all around me except when I sleep, fortunately!","sp":"M","part":1,"t":1039,"tOriginal":1080,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Nelson, what is the most important aspect of building a great character?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1132,"tOriginal":1087.1,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Many things: life experience, including weird eating habits, and then physical aspects are also extremely important.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1138,"tOriginal":1096.7,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"We are constantly doing things with our bodies that reflect the way that we feel and what we think.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1146.7,"tOriginal":1109.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Now, a more specific question.","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1157,"tOriginal":1124.5,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Do you write an outline before you actually start writing?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1159.6,"tOriginal":1128.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Sometimes.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1165,"tOriginal":1136.4,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"I don't particularly like doing it, but certain stories demand it.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1166.1,"tOriginal":1138,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"You'd like to ask you about your favourite films.","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1172,"tOriginal":1146.7,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"What type of structure do these films usually have?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1176,"tOriginal":1153.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"They completely vary.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1180,"tOriginal":1161,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Different films have vastly different structures.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1181.6,"tOriginal":1163.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"I love the structure in some films: instead of starting at the beginning and going until the end, it starts in the middle, and goes backwards and forwards.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1184.8,"tOriginal":1168.1,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Very interesting.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1200,"tOriginal":1190.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"During the writing process, do you ever find that your characters start to speak for themselves?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1201,"tOriginal":1191.9,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Always.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1209,"tOriginal":1204.6,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"If they don't speak for themselves, then I'm sure I've done something wrong.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1210,"tOriginal":1206.2,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Does dialogue come easily, or is it difficult for you?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1216,"tOriginal":1216.6,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"No!","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1222,"tOriginal":1224.5,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"None of it comes easily.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1223.1,"tOriginal":1226.1,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"It's all painful.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1225.7,"tOriginal":1230.1,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Everything in writing a script is very, very hard.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1227.2,"tOriginal":1232.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"What about your daily routine when you're writing?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1232,"tOriginal":1239.6,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Do you have one?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1235.3,"tOriginal":1245.9,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Working out is a huge part of it.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1237,"tOriginal":1249.1,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"I do boxing and yoga.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1240.8,"tOriginal":1255.5,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"I go to the gym, but I'm not very fond of jogging.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1243.1,"tOriginal":1259.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Other things that also help are putting my phone away, turning it off and leaving it in another room, and listening to music sometimes.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1248.8,"tOriginal":1269,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Have you ever experienced writer's block?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1260,"tOriginal":1288,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"That is, have you ever found yourself totally unable to write?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1263.9,"tOriginal":1292.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Oh yes!","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1271,"tOriginal":1301.5,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"I think it happens to all writers, and it's really awful!","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1271.8,"tOriginal":1303.1,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"You sit in front of the computer, hour after hour, and you don't write a single word.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1276.3,"tOriginal":1311.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Very frustrating.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1283.3,"tOriginal":1325.3,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Very depressing.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1284.2,"tOriginal":1326.9,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"How did you overcome it?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1285,"tOriginal":1328.5,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Well, I have to admit that I've tried a lot of things: keeping a strict routine, meditation, writing on paper, using a notebook, working with colleagues.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1288,"tOriginal":1332.5,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Finally, what worked for me was camping a few days alone in the woods.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1301,"tOriginal":1353.1,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"When I came back, I could write again.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1308,"tOriginal":1364.2,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"How interesting!","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1312,"tOriginal":1370.6,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Screenwriting is obviously a solitary job.","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1313,"tOriginal":1372.2,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"How do you deal with it?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1316,"tOriginal":1377,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Is it hard to be alone so much?","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1319,"tOriginal":1381.7,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"As a matter of fact, I like being alone and working alone, although it can get hard sometimes.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1323,"tOriginal":1388.1,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"When you work in an office, you can discuss things with people, or even get mad at them.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1330.5,"tOriginal":1402.4,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"But when you work alone, you have to do all these things with yourself!","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1337.9,"tOriginal":1416.7,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"But it's not really a problem for me.","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1343.7,"tOriginal":1427.8,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"Well, I'm glad to hear that, Nelson.","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1347,"tOriginal":1434.1,"tSource":"word-anchor"},{"en":"Thank you very much for talking to us on the show.","sp":"W","part":2,"t":1349.7,"tOriginal":1439.7,"tSource":"anchor-interpolated"},{"en":"You're welcome!","sp":"M","part":2,"t":1354,"tOriginal":1448.4,"tSource":"word-anchor"}]},"2024":{"A":[{"en":"Test for English. majors 2024 grade eight, part one listening comprehension section a mini lecture.","t":14.93,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":[1,2]},{"en":"In this section you hear a mini lecture ture once only.","t":28.25,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":3},{"en":"While listening to the mini lecture, complete the gap filling task on answer sheet one and write no more than three words for each gap.","t":35.47,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":4},{"en":"Make sure what you fill in is both grammatically and semantically acceptable.","t":44.49,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":5},{"en":"You may use the blank sheet for note taking.","t":47.11,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":6},{"en":"You have 30s to preview the gap filling task.","t":50.11,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":7},{"en":"Now listen to the mini lecture.","t":89.99,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":8},{"en":"When it is over, you will be given three minutes to check your work.","t":92.99,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":9},{"en":"Why is it harder to learn a 2nd language?","t":98.59,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":10},{"en":"Good morning, everyone.","t":103.09,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":11},{"en":"In our last lecture, we discussed briefly 1st language acquisition.","t":105.07,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":12},{"en":"We have learned that we are born to process and produce natural human language by looking at what we are exposed to or what we create with the universal grammar principles that we are born with.","t":110.43,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":13},{"en":"We also know that we acquire our native language in a natural way.","t":116.97,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":14},{"en":"However, if you have had the experience of trying to master a 2nd language, no doubt you find it to be a challenge quite unlike your 1st language experience, because there are important differences between acquiring a 1st language and learning a 2nd one.","t":127.13,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":15},{"en":"So in today's lecture, I will discuss why it is harder to learn a 2nd language by comparing the differences and similarities between these two ways of language processing.","t":146.37,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":16},{"en":"And I'll finish by briefly mentioning a related topic, that is language translation.","t":153.97,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":17},{"en":"Now let's come to the differences 1st.","t":163.29,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":18},{"en":"First of all, as everybody knows, anyone who is learning a 2nd language has already acquired a 1st language, right?","t":166.79,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":19},{"en":"So the language mechanism in the brain has already had certain linguistic parameters set, such as word order in the 1st language.","t":176.35,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":20},{"en":"And that makes 2nd language learning quite different.","t":185.19,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":21},{"en":"What one needs to learn are the specific rules of the 2nd language, which is often called the target language.","t":188.89,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":22},{"en":"In 2nd language learning, the 1st language tends to serve as a model, and mistakes often result from taking words from the target language and putting them together, because learners tend to apply rules from the 1st language.","t":196.25,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":23},{"en":"For example, if the 1st language is English, the target language is Korean, a 2nd language learner might position the Korean verb between the subject and the object of the sentence using the English word order, rather than placing the verb after the object, which is the correct Korean word order.","t":211.75,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":24},{"en":"Generally speaking, the greater the difference between the 1st language and the target language, the more tasks are involved in learning the latter.","t":232.73,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":25},{"en":"What's more, 2nd language learning can even be characterized as a gradual shift from the 1st language orientation to the target language orientation.","t":241.95,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":26},{"en":"Okay, let's come to the 2nd point.","t":252.39,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":27},{"en":"As we all know, 1st language acquisition typically takes place in early childhood at a very Young age.","t":254.83,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":28},{"en":"However, 2nd language learning, especially in a classroom setting, proceeds more quickly with adults and adolescents than with younger children initially, although at the end of the day, it is the younger child who will become more proficient in 2nd language learning than grown ups.","t":263.41,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":29},{"en":"That is to say, even in 2nd language learning, age is also a major factor.","t":281.77,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":30},{"en":"As in 1st language acquisition, the 3rd point I want to bring up here is that it's apparent that 1st language acquisition happens without conscious teaching, you know in a kind of natural way, as I mentioned just now.","t":287.39,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":31},{"en":"But the 2nd language learning generally does not.","t":302.45,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":32},{"en":"Numerous studies have shown that a number of traits such as self confidence, motivation, good self image and low anxiety can facilitate 2nd language learning, but none of these traits seem as important to 1st language acquisition.","t":305.11,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":33},{"en":"Okay, let's move to the 4th point.","t":325.03,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":34},{"en":"Studies have shown that the input that affects 2nd language learning is more complex then that in a 1st language acquisition context.","t":327.33,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":35},{"en":"What do I mean here?","t":337.21,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":36},{"en":"Now, let me give you an example.","t":338.95,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":37},{"en":"If a 2nd language learner has a classroom teacher who talks in the target language at a quick rate in complex sentences and about complicated matters, the learner will probably have a harder time in the learning process.","t":341.19,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":38},{"en":"However, 1st language acquisition can proceed at the same rate whether or not adults simplify their language.","t":355.85,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":39},{"en":"Now, the 5th point is that practice is important for 2nd language learning, but not so much for 1st language acquisition.","t":364.73,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":40},{"en":"Even very quiet children, I mean kids who don't like to talk to people, can acquire their 1st language at the ordinary rate, but that doesn't work for a 2nd language learner.","t":372.63,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":41},{"en":"For example, he or she has to constantly practice listening and speaking in order to be proficient in that language.","t":384.07,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":42},{"en":"This means that 2nd language learners need to put in a lot more effort.","t":392.19,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":43},{"en":"Despite the differences I've mentioned between 1st language acquisition and 2nd language learning, they also share a few similarities.","t":397.59,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":44},{"en":"Let's take a look at them. 1st is the learning speed. 2nd language learning can proceed as quickly as 1st language acquisition.","t":406.43,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":45},{"en":"If the target language is used as the medium of instruction, then the next is language exposure, which is both important in the two processes.","t":415.21,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":46},{"en":"As in 1st language acquisition, 2nd language learning can be more successful when richly interactive language is used in the classroom.","t":417.19,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":47},{"en":"That is, exposure to authentic language, be it oral or written, is a better teaching strategy than memorization, drills or recitations.","t":434.71,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":48},{"en":"So far, I've taken you through some of the differences and similarities between 1st language acquisition and 2nd language learning.","t":445.87,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":49},{"en":"You may find 2nd language learning is to some extent, a much harder process than 1st language acquisition.","t":447.13,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":50},{"en":"A final point here, which is closely related to 2nd language learning, that is, language translation.","t":458.45,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":51},{"en":"In language learning classes, you are often asked to translate between languages as a form of exercise or assessment, and you may have already faced challenges when transforming one language into the other.","t":468.55,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":52},{"en":"There is an Italian saying which goes something like this, translators, traitors.","t":482.99,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":53},{"en":"What it really means is that translation can never be perfect.","t":488.21,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":54},{"en":"So anyone who translates necessarily betrays the original, more or less.","t":493.27,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":55},{"en":"In my opinion, translation is not a mechanical act.","t":499.01,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":56},{"en":"Rather, translation is a creative act.","t":502.77,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":57},{"en":"Some have even said that translating is rewriting.","t":504.71,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":58},{"en":"Different translators will offer different translations of the same text, and these different translations have their own strengths and drawbacks.","t":510.17,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":59},{"en":"So in my next lecture, we'll discuss the complexity of language translation.","t":519.21,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":60},{"en":"Thank you.","t":522.1,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":61},{"en":"Now you have three minutes to check your work.","t":524.99,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":62}],"B":[{"en":"This is the end of section a mini lecture.","t":711.07,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":63,"part":1},{"en":"Section b interview.","t":712.41,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":64,"part":1},{"en":"In this section, you will hear two interviews.","t":717.89,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":65,"part":1},{"en":"At the end of each interview, five questions will be asked about what was said.","t":720.51,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":66,"part":1},{"en":"Both the interviews and the questions will be read once only.","t":726.79,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":67,"part":1},{"en":"After each question, there will be a 10s pause.","t":731.47,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":68,"part":1},{"en":"During the pause, you should read the four choices of A, B, C, and d, and mark the best answer to each question.","t":735.91,"tSource":"asr2","tCueNo":69,"part":1},{"en":"On answer sheet two, you have 30s to preview the choices.","t":738.91,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":70,"part":1},{"en":"Now listen to the 1st interview.","t":780.16,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":71,"part":1},{"en":"Questions one to five are based on the 1st interview.","t":781.39,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":72,"part":1},{"en":"Hello, Barry.","t":788.34,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":73,"part":1},{"en":"Nice to have you on our program.","t":789.58,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":74,"part":1},{"en":"Thanks.","t":790.68,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":75,"part":1},{"en":"Now you've.","t":791.13,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":76,"part":1},{"en":"enjoyed a very successful career as one of the leading public intellectuals and commentators on current and global events, and also as one of the most distinguished contemporary novelists.","t":791.58,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":77,"part":1},{"en":"What do you think of your two.","t":806.64,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":78,"part":1},{"en":"activities?","t":807.84,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":79,"part":1},{"en":"Well, since I have two brains, I have two ways of writing, that is, literary creation and critical writing.","t":808.36,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":80,"part":1},{"en":"I like them equally well.","t":817.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":81,"part":1},{"en":"This, as a matter of fact, allows for a rotation which lets one brain rest while the other.","t":820.04,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":82,"part":1},{"en":"one works.","t":826.02,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":83,"part":1},{"en":"Okay, then, which of the two activities, fiction or essay writing, do you find more demanding and more satisfying?","t":827.0,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":84,"part":1},{"en":"Well, everything is difficult in the writing of a book, whether it is fiction or theory.","t":834.82,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":85,"part":1},{"en":"But I'd say writing fiction is probably more arduous because you have to create a completely new world and not just comment on an existing one.","t":842.88,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":86,"part":1},{"en":"It offers a complete universe which holds your interest throughout the novel and hopefully will leave a lasting impression.","t":854.24,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":87,"part":1},{"en":"So I wonder if a good novel doesn't endure longer than an essay because the essay is limited to the time in which it is written.","t":862.6,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":88,"part":1},{"en":"In any case, producing both of these at once is an aesthetic risk, because you can be disowned by both camps.","t":869.78,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":89,"part":1},{"en":"Your work can be considered not serious enough for the philosophers and too theoretical for the novelists.","t":880.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":90,"part":1},{"en":"But I like generating new things in this way.","t":887.48,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":91,"part":1},{"en":"Hmm, now let's focus on fiction writing.","t":891.0,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":92,"part":1},{"en":"From your point of view, are there any themes and subjects that are are particularly appropriate to.","t":895.8,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":93,"part":1},{"en":"fiction writing?","t":901.94,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":94,"part":1},{"en":"Well, I'd like to say novels and essays treat similar themes, but from a different viewpoint.","t":903.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":95,"part":1},{"en":"For me, novel writing is characterized by a search for extremes.","t":910.94,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":96,"part":1},{"en":"It is always an attempt to escape from oneself, from the conventions, from professional and familial success.","t":915.46,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":97,"part":1},{"en":"We only write well in the grip of emotion.","t":925.02,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":98,"part":1},{"en":"And the novel speaks a truth that would be inaudible in an essay.","t":927.96,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":99,"part":1},{"en":"And then the essay, it leads back to the idea of reality.","t":931.9,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":100,"part":1},{"en":"But the novel frees us from it.","t":938.22,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":101,"part":1},{"en":"It expresses an urge toward disorder, toward fantasy, which goes beyond normal limits.","t":940.52,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":102,"part":1},{"en":"Okay, you write with great clarity in your novels.","t":946.42,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":103,"part":1},{"en":"If you were to single out novels, which ones do you find especially inspirational or compelling?","t":951.96,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":104,"part":1},{"en":"It's only through clarity that we achieve depth in fiction writing.","t":957.36,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":105,"part":1},{"en":"I am attracted to very different genres, for example, the magic realism of South America, the literature of ancient China and central Europe, the Gothic novels and certain works of science fiction.","t":963.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":106,"part":1},{"en":"And it is often minor novels which have impressed me the longest.","t":972.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":107,"part":1},{"en":"Barry, another question for you.","t":981.58,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":108,"part":1},{"en":"Given our increasingly visual and mediatized culture, how do you see the future of fiction writing?","t":985.38,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":109,"part":1},{"en":"Our country remains one of those rare countries where people still buy lots of books, many more than elsewhere.","t":992.44,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":110,"part":1},{"en":"So it's a marvelous place for writers.","t":1001.0,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":111,"part":1},{"en":"As a result, novels proliferate here, just like rabbits.","t":1004.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":112,"part":1},{"en":"Everyone wants to write.","t":1008.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":113,"part":1},{"en":"Literature isn't threatened by becoming a rarity, but rather by obesity.","t":1010.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":114,"part":1},{"en":"Excuse me, what do you mean by obesity?","t":1014.4,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":115,"part":1},{"en":"Well, we're reaching a situation in which there are more writers than readers. 700 novels were published in September last year and 500 in January this year.","t":1018.38,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":116,"part":1},{"en":"This has caused the public to turn away in confusion.","t":1029.96,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":117,"part":1},{"en":"But let's not complain about this excess of books.","t":1035.78,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":118,"part":1},{"en":"The point is, how can we find our way around?","t":1039.22,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":119,"part":1},{"en":"I think there are still a few alternatives.","t":1043.04,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":120,"part":1},{"en":"For example, to stick to the classics, to follow the list of bestsellers of the moment, or to collect a private library of books, one that you share with special friends.","t":1045.4,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":121,"part":1},{"en":"Actually, we usually mix these three alternatives.","t":1058.5,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":122,"part":1},{"en":"Thank you very, Barry, for coming to talk on our program.","t":1062.42,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":123,"part":1},{"en":"Pleasure.","t":1065.64,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":124,"part":1},{"en":"This is the end of the 1st interview.","t":1069.12,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":125,"part":1},{"en":"Questions one to five are based on what you have just heard.","t":1072.2,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":126,"part":1},{"en":"Question one, how does the man feel about fiction writing?","t":1075.28,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":127,"part":1},{"en":"Question two, what does the man say about the essay?","t":1092.69,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":128,"part":1},{"en":"Question three, according to the man, what is the similarity between novels and essays?","t":1107.23,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":129,"part":1},{"en":"Question four, what is the man's most favorite type of novels?","t":1124.32,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":130,"part":1},{"en":"Question five, according to the man, what will be the future of fiction writing?","t":1140.55,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":131,"part":1},{"en":"Now listen to the 2nd interview.","t":1156.62,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":132,"part":2},{"en":"Questions six to ten are based on the 2nd interview.","t":1157.88,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":133,"part":2},{"en":"Antarctica, a continent of snow and ice, is now losing ice three times faster than it was in 2007.","t":1165.02,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":134,"part":2},{"en":"In a new study published last week in the Journal nature, more than 80 scientists from multiple countries used satellite data to examine the Antarctica's vast ice sheets.","t":1172.04,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":135,"part":2},{"en":"And their prediction is that if the current rate of ice melt continues, sea levels could rise six inches by the year 20 100.","t":1187.16,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":136,"part":2},{"en":"Joining us today for more on this study and the consequences of sea level rise is Benjamin Johnson, president and CEO of climate watch.","t":1197.18,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":137,"part":2},{"en":"So Ben, we've heard about sea level rise for years.","t":1207.92,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":138,"part":2},{"en":"How significant is this particular study and what did it look at?","t":1211.7,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":139,"part":2},{"en":"Well, the 1st thing I'd like to point out is Antarctica is just one part of the story.","t":1215.5,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":140,"part":2},{"en":"That is to say, we have six inches of contribution from Antarctica if it continues to shed ice at the rate it was measured.","t":1223.04,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":141,"part":2},{"en":"But but there are other sources as well.","t":1231.4,"tSource":"asr2","tCueNo":142,"part":2},{"en":"So altogether, we would be looking at three feet.","t":1232.78,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":143,"part":2},{"en":"three feet of sea level rise by the year 20 100.","t":1240.62,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":144,"part":2},{"en":"That is consequential to hundreds of millions of people that live in coastal cities all over the planet.","t":1246.3,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":145,"part":2},{"en":"Yes, it is.","t":1251.92,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":146,"part":2},{"en":"We're already seeing floods increase.","t":1254.54,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":147,"part":2},{"en":"Yesterday, for example, floods in some of the areas around the country.","t":1257.4,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":148,"part":2},{"en":"And these floods wouldn't have happened without the sea level rise that we've already seen.","t":1263.5,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":149,"part":2},{"en":"Yeah and what is it that is convincing these scientists that the rates are changing?","t":1269.3,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":150,"part":2},{"en":"What are they studying?","t":1270.62,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":151,"part":2},{"en":"What are they looking at?","t":1277.08,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":152,"part":2},{"en":"How can they tell?","t":1278.03,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":153,"part":2},{"en":"Well.","t":1278.51,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":154,"part":2},{"en":"they have a lot of direct measurements from satellites of the height of the surface of the ice sheets, so they're able to see how that height changes over time.","t":1278.98,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":155,"part":2},{"en":"These satellites also measure the gravitational pool of the ice sheet, and therefore the scientists know how much ice is there.","t":1292.96,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":156,"part":2},{"en":"So those are the two main forms of measurement.","t":1303.44,"tSource":"asr2","tCueNo":157,"part":2},{"en":"I know that there are climate science deniers who say, look at the east side of Antarctica.","t":1307.72,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":158,"part":2},{"en":"It looks on a map.","t":1313.88,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":159,"part":2},{"en":"There's actually more ice coming in.","t":1315.04,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":160,"part":2},{"en":"Doesn't this all balance itself out?","t":1317.46,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":161,"part":2},{"en":"We do anticipate that in the future, snowfall will increase in East Antarctica, and I hope so.","t":1320.4,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":162,"part":2},{"en":"But this study shows over recent decades it hasn't.","t":1327.9,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":163,"part":2},{"en":"Does it mean that if nothing is going to change, areas around on coastal waterways will be severely impacted?","t":1331.08,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":164,"part":2},{"en":"Yeah if we continue to see the ice melt speeding up and don't cut back on our climate pollution, emissions, then we're pointed more towards six feet possibly rather than the three feet predicted by 20 100.","t":1338.9,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":165,"part":2},{"en":"And that will be unmanageable in very many places.","t":1343.68,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":166,"part":2},{"en":"Also the effects that were seeing of sea level rise, of climate change in a global capacity.","t":1359.28,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":167,"part":2},{"en":"This is because of the carbon that we've already put into the atmosphere, not just exactly what we're doing today.","t":1365.36,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":168,"part":2},{"en":"So even if everyone stopped driving, all the factories shut down, and somehow we didn't produce co two, we're still going to see the effects.","t":1372.56,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":169,"part":2},{"en":"of climate change.","t":1381.06,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":170,"part":2},{"en":"Yes, we are.","t":1382.62,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":171,"part":2},{"en":"Unfortunately, once the carbon is in the atmosphere, most of it stays for hundreds and thousands of years.","t":1384.2,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":172,"part":2},{"en":"But if we do something to control our pollution now, we can really slow it down a lot and make it more manageable.","t":1390.82,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":173,"part":2},{"en":"And that's the name of the game.","t":1397.84,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":174,"part":2},{"en":"Really.","t":1402.48,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":175,"part":2},{"en":"Slower change will be much more manageable than the fast change that is possible.","t":1403.82,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":176,"part":2},{"en":"All right, Ben, thank you so much for talking to us.","t":1409.12,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":177,"part":2},{"en":"Pleasure.","t":1412.88,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":178,"part":2},{"en":"This is the end of the 2nd interview.","t":1415.86,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":179,"part":2},{"en":"Questions six to ten are based on what you have just heard.","t":1419.13,"tSource":"interp","tCueNo":180,"part":2},{"en":"Question six, how much does Antarctica contribute to sea level rise?","t":1422.4,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":181,"part":2},{"en":"Question seven, what makes scientists believe that the rising rates are changing?","t":1440.22,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":182,"part":2},{"en":"Question eight, what does the man expect to see in East Antarctica in the future?","t":1456.23,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":183,"part":2},{"en":"Question nine, what measure should be taken to slow down ice melting?","t":1472.15,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":184,"part":2},{"en":"Question ten, what is the main topic of the interview?","t":1488.04,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":185,"part":2},{"en":"This is the end of section b interview.","t":1501.78,"tSource":"anchor","tCueNo":186,"part":2},{"en":"This is the end of part one listening comprehension.","t":1505.8,"tSource":"asr","tCueNo":187,"part":2}]}};
